    {
      "id": "pswSKYvIfIXhrWPL-levm",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -5445.162282269786,
      "y": -2745.1521687724535,
      "width": 1196.3592529296875,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "w2p0C7PxHocij1rwyX1el",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1175544691,
      "version": 1826,
      "versionNonce": 1787321079,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785297553949,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Situation, Task, Action Result\n2. Answer with specific examples of what i've done with concrete details leveraging the technologies used and their impact\n    2.1 Signal and narrate your resume's Google XYZ structure\n3. Audience must receive the signal you are prepared to do the job (not learn on the job)\n4. Philosophies of Code\n    - ...-driven-development\n        - business, test, type, domain\n    - assume users don't have ill-intent (happy path), minimum effective security\n    - leave code better than you found it, be empathetic to the developer who originally made it",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Situation, Task, Action Result\n2. Answer with specific examples of what i've done with concrete details leveraging the technologies used and their impact\n    2.1 Signal and narrate your resume's Google XYZ structure\n3. Audience must receive the signal you are prepared to do the job (not learn on the job)\n4. Philosophies of Code\n    - ...-driven-development\n        - business, test, type, domain\n    - assume users don't have ill-intent (happy path), minimum effective security\n    - leave code better than you found it, be empathetic to the developer who originally made it",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b2J"
    },
    {
      "id": "060SOwl0fkvqYrJ82ttsl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -5442.020946042652,
      "y": -2412.7895128788955,
      "width": 639.9796752929688,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "w2p0C7PxHocij1rwyX1el",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1731430779,
      "version": 694,
      "versionNonce": 1181973495,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785297555257,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Key Coaching Point\n• Stay out of hypotheticals (\"I would...\", \"I could...\", \"I imagine...\")\n• Lead with what you have actually done\n• If you lack direct experience:\no Clearly state it\no Explain related exposure\no Demonstrate foundational knowledge",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Key Coaching Point\n• Stay out of hypotheticals (\"I would...\", \"I could...\", \"I imagine...\")\n• Lead with what you have actually done\n• If you lack direct experience:\no Clearly state it\no Explain related exposure\no Demonstrate foundational knowledge",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b2K"
    },
    {
      "id": "0GN-o-SVepucuE7EYb7aH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -5088.42244933047,
      "y": -4147.375940771679,
      "width": 902.6194458007812,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "w2p0C7PxHocij1rwyX1el",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1967602843,
      "version": 595,
      "versionNonce": 1103905943,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785297542798,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Answer Framework\n• What was the project/problem?\n• What specifically was your role?\n• What technologies did you use?\n• What was the outcome/impact?\n• If limited experience: \"I haven't directly owned that, but I've worked with/alongside X and\nhave been building knowledge in Y.\"",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Answer Framework\n• What was the project/problem?\n• What specifically was your role?\n• What technologies did you use?\n• What was the outcome/impact?\n• If limited experience: \"I haven't directly owned that, but I've worked with/alongside X and\nhave been building knowledge in Y.\"",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b2L"
    },
    {
      "id": "stY-3ZkBEm8M3GIeWt4Fe",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -5086.553260709338,
      "y": -3919.0321614152335,
      "width": 661.439453125,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "w2p0C7PxHocij1rwyX1el",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1063901173,
      "version": 552,
      "versionNonce": 858102199,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785297542798,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Python Experience\n• Be prepared with 2-3 examples\n\n• APIs, backend services, automation, integrations, data processing\n• Discuss architecture, challenges, and business impact",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Python Experience\n• Be prepared with 2-3 examples\n\n• APIs, backend services, automation, integrations, data processing\n• Discuss architecture, challenges, and business impact",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b2M"
    },
    {
      "id": "SSg8TwEoGZEgn2xleju9E",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -10598.780026265917,
      "y": -4184.819202996978,
      "width": 923.3179582894181,
      "height": 66.15167348553688,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "w2p0C7PxHocij1rwyX1el",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1742505211,
      "version": 854,
      "versionNonce": 506882775,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785297548749,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Use real examples whenever possible",
      "fontSize": 52.921338788429495,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Use real examples whenever possible",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b2N"
    },
    {
      "id": "yFRbXxU3F7u7zlft1pHZ_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -5475.261185951445,
      "y": -2076.138203764319,
      "width": 667.799560546875,
      "height": 325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "w2p0C7PxHocij1rwyX1el",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1141462971,
      "version": 669,
      "versionNonce": 150866743,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785297556299,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Phrases to Use\n• \"My direct experience was...\"\n• \"I partnered closely with...\"\n• \"My level of ownership was...\"\n• \"I haven't directly done X, but I've gained exposure through...\"\n• \"That's an area I'm actively looking to deepen.\"\n\nPhrases to Avoid\n• \"I would...\"\n• \"I could...\"\n• \"If I were...\"\n• \"I've been exposed to...\" (without explaining what exposure means)\n• Any statement that blurs ownership vs participation",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Phrases to Use\n• \"My direct experience was...\"\n• \"I partnered closely with...\"\n• \"My level of ownership was...\"\n• \"I haven't directly done X, but I've gained exposure through...\"\n• \"That's an area I'm actively looking to deepen.\"\n\nPhrases to Avoid\n• \"I would...\"\n• \"I could...\"\n• \"If I were...\"\n• \"I've been exposed to...\" (without explaining what exposure means)\n• Any statement that blurs ownership vs participation",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b2O"
    },
    {
      "id": "fTsi7QQrbhmahxB3F07Qe",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -5079.426205066827,
      "y": -3718.794470184975,
      "width": 770.739501953125,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "w2p0C7PxHocij1rwyX1el",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1829315445,
      "version": 555,
      "versionNonce": 1426440471,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785297542798,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Final Reminder\n• Credibility > Perfection\n• Ownership > Buzzwords\n• Clarity > Overexplaining\n• Honest about gaps + ambitious about growth = strongest interview outcome.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Final Reminder\n• Credibility > Perfection\n• Ownership > Buzzwords\n• Clarity > Overexplaining\n• Honest about gaps + ambitious about growth = strongest interview outcome.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b2P"
    },
    {
      "id": "0IECfJnwA-OVAAylWU7Cx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -6079.753630400771,
      "y": -3657.4739686306093,
      "width": 1623.4786376953125,
      "height": 750,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "w2p0C7PxHocij1rwyX1el",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1135695707,
      "version": 2625,
      "versionNonce": 184256055,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785297542798,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Absstract to agnostic frameworks systems thinking but explain from hardware 1st principles\n    * STAR\n    * end-to-end\n        - design, data, backend, model, frontend, deploy\n\nReal example:\n    Q: how would you improve performance of a pipeline\n    A: what non-functional characteristic am I improving? When running TPU computing for weeks, high availbility is imporant\n    Q: improve the latency for a data pipeline\n    A: (real responses live in the moment with limited time; joined late and hard cut off with time back)\n        - selecting too much data\n        - chunking strategies could be improved\n        - if we could use GPU, should we?\n            - CPU--i/o--GPU & clustering\n        - hardware limit to vertical computing, consider horizontal strategies\n            - consider concurrent workflows with sharding and/or parralleism for distributive compute\n        - financial constraints, sometimes you can't because of other constraints so set expectations with stakeholders\n        \nAfter some thoughts:\n    - interviewier and recruiter communicated real-examples. This interviewier and others in the past don't want hypotheticals. Signal real answers from real experience.\n    - additional approaches: memory management for less data bloat to compute faster and/or improved reads-speed\n        - improving reads by structuring data as columns instead of rows\n        - SQL Joins could be improved, Python immutability & memory/garbage management, otherwise refactor to C/C++/Rust or some other performative language\n            - database selection and other systems design considerations holistically (batch vs streaming)\n        - zero-copy (no i/o handoff between CPU/GPU and within CPU L1/L2 memory)\n        - distributive compute with clusters\n    \n    - similar to monolith vs microservices is partitioning vs sharding\n        - single: monolith, partitioning strategies (like additional subfolders in a folder)\n        - multiple: microservices, sharding",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Absstract to agnostic frameworks systems thinking but explain from hardware 1st principles\n    * STAR\n    * end-to-end\n        - design, data, backend, model, frontend, deploy\n\nReal example:\n    Q: how would you improve performance of a pipeline\n    A: what non-functional characteristic am I improving? When running TPU computing for weeks, high availbility is imporant\n    Q: improve the latency for a data pipeline\n    A: (real responses live in the moment with limited time; joined late and hard cut off with time back)\n        - selecting too much data\n        - chunking strategies could be improved\n        - if we could use GPU, should we?\n            - CPU--i/o--GPU & clustering\n        - hardware limit to vertical computing, consider horizontal strategies\n            - consider concurrent workflows with sharding and/or parralleism for distributive compute\n        - financial constraints, sometimes you can't because of other constraints so set expectations with stakeholders\n        \nAfter some thoughts:\n    - interviewier and recruiter communicated real-examples. This interviewier and others in the past don't want hypotheticals. Signal real answers from real experience.\n    - additional approaches: memory management for less data bloat to compute faster and/or improved reads-speed\n        - improving reads by structuring data as columns instead of rows\n        - SQL Joins could be improved, Python immutability & memory/garbage management, otherwise refactor to C/C++/Rust or some other performative language\n            - database selection and other systems design considerations holistically (batch vs streaming)\n        - zero-copy (no i/o handoff between CPU/GPU and within CPU L1/L2 memory)\n        - distributive compute with clusters\n    \n    - similar to monolith vs microservices is partitioning vs sharding\n        - single: monolith, partitioning strategies (like additional subfolders in a folder)\n        - multiple: microservices, sharding",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b2Q"
    },
    {
      "id": "TgcvJsQqQzqWDODd8nMBv",
