      "updated": 1784739795302,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Pro Git (Scott Chacon & Ben Straub) — free official book at git-scm.com/book; the canonical deep dive on rebasing, bisect, and git internals beyond daily-driver usage.\n- Learn Git Branching (learngitbranching.js.org) — interactive visual sandbox for practicing interactive rebase, cherry-pick, and merge-conflict resolution without risking a real repo.\n- Google Engineering Practices (google.github.io/eng-practices) — official \"How to do a code review\" and \"The CL Author's Guide,\" the most widely cited public standard for review culture.\n- Staff Engineer archetypes & guides (staffeng.com) — Will Larson's site on staff-plus scope and influence: Tech Lead, Architect, Solver, and Right Hand archetypes.\n- The Pragmatic Engineer (newsletter.pragmaticengineer.com) — Gergely Orosz's newsletter on career progression and real-world engineering practice at senior/staff level.\n- levels.fyi — crowdsourced leveling and compensation data across companies; useful for calibrating what \"senior\" actually means from one company's ladder to another's.\n- Blind (teamblind.com) — anonymous, verified-employee community for compensation, interview-loop, and leveling discussions; read critically, since it's unmoderated.\n- Tech Interview Handbook (techinterviewhandbook.org) — free, community-maintained guide covering behavioral prep, negotiation, and the end-to-end interview process, not just algorithms.\n- Pramp, now part of Exponent (pramp.com) — free peer-to-peer mock interview practice for rehearsing live problem-solving and communication under time pressure.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Pro Git (Scott Chacon & Ben Straub) — free official book at git-scm.com/book; the canonical deep dive on rebasing, bisect, and git internals beyond daily-driver usage.\n- Learn Git Branching (learngitbranching.js.org) — interactive visual sandbox for practicing interactive rebase, cherry-pick, and merge-conflict resolution without risking a real repo.\n- Google Engineering Practices (google.github.io/eng-practices) — official \"How to do a code review\" and \"The CL Author's Guide,\" the most widely cited public standard for review culture.\n- Staff Engineer archetypes & guides (staffeng.com) — Will Larson's site on staff-plus scope and influence: Tech Lead, Architect, Solver, and Right Hand archetypes.\n- The Pragmatic Engineer (newsletter.pragmaticengineer.com) — Gergely Orosz's newsletter on career progression and real-world engineering practice at senior/staff level.\n- levels.fyi — crowdsourced leveling and compensation data across companies; useful for calibrating what \"senior\" actually means from one company's ladder to another's.\n- Blind (teamblind.com) — anonymous, verified-employee community for compensation, interview-loop, and leveling discussions; read critically, since it's unmoderated.\n- Tech Interview Handbook (techinterviewhandbook.org) — free, community-maintained guide covering behavioral prep, negotiation, and the end-to-end interview process, not just algorithms.\n- Pramp, now part of Exponent (pramp.com) — free peer-to-peer mock interview practice for rehearsing live problem-solving and communication under time pressure.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b33"
